      "matchText": "Bozo",
      "term": "Bozo",
      "definition": "A West African people known above all as masters of the Niger River — fishermen and boat-builders of the Inner Niger Delta whose lives are organized around the water. Under the Mali Empire they kept their language and river-bound way of life while becoming imperial subjects."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Crusader",
      "term": "Crusader state",
      "definition": "A territory carved out and ruled by Western European Crusaders, most of them established in the eastern Mediterranean and the lands of the former Byzantine Empire after the Crusades. The Latin Empire of Constantinople, built on the wreckage of the Fourth Crusade's sack of the Byzantine capital, was one of them."
    }
